\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {36}{\ignorespaces Second FE-side consistency check reproduced from the presentation: starting from the shell-model reaction moment $M_f=\SI {10.0927}{\kilo \newton \metre }$ and the piping-code coefficient $B_2=4.371$, the equivalent elastic reference stress is reconstructed as $\sigma _{0,\mathrm  {ref}}=0.79\,B_2\,M_f/Z=\SI {258.938}{MPa}$. Solving the coupled elastic-follow-up and Ramberg--Osgood relations shown on the slide then gives $\sigma _{3,\mathrm  {est}}=\SI {112.6}{MPa}$ and $g=0.435$, i.e.\ the reaction-based FE abatement coefficient $g_{\mathrm  {reaction}}=0.436$ to within rounding.}}{29}{figure.caption.43}\protected@file@percent }
